# {{NAME}} Agent Instructions

This workspace manages Proxmox VMs and containers.

## Default VM/CT Setup Flow

When asked to create a VM or container:

1. Load the `proxmox` skill before acting.
2. Ask only for missing blocking information (VM ID, node, memory, disk).
3. Run `manager-setup/scripts/bootstrap-item.sh <vm-name> --vmid <id> --type <vm|ct>`.
4. Continue configuration until done.
5. Run `manager-setup/scripts/update-inventory.sh` before finishing.
6. Report the VM ID, node, and what was configured.

## Defaults

- Owner: {{OWNER}}
- Node: pve
- Type: vm
- Memory: 2048 MB
- Disk: 20G
- OS: ubuntu-22.04

## Blocking Questions

Ask before continuing when missing:

- VM/CT name
- VM ID (must be unique in Proxmox)
- Proxmox node hostname or IP

## Inventory Requirement

The root `README.md` inventory is the source of truth. Always update it after any VM/CT change.
